# 35. Interview Questions

## Q1. What is CSS?

CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets. It is used to style and design HTML elements.

---

## Q2. What is the difference between HTML and CSS?

HTML creates the structure of a webpage.

CSS controls its appearance and layout.

---

## Q3. What is the CSS Box Model?

The CSS Box Model consists of:

    Content
    Padding
    Border
    Margin

---

## Q4. Difference between padding and margin?

Padding is the space inside an element.

Margin is the space outside an element.

---

## Q5. What is Flexbox?

Flexbox is a CSS layout system used to arrange elements in rows or columns.

---

## Q6. What does `display: flex` do?

It makes an element a Flexbox container and allows its children to be arranged using Flexbox properties.

---

## Q7. What does `justify-content` do?

It aligns Flexbox items along the main axis.

---

## Q8. What does `align-items` do?

It aligns Flexbox items along the cross axis.

---

## Q9. What is `gap`?

`gap` creates space between Flexbox or Grid items.

---

## Q10. What is `flex-wrap`?

It allows Flexbox items to move to another line when there isn't enough space.

---

## Q11. What is `:hover`?

`:hover` applies CSS when the mouse pointer is over an element.

---

## Q12. Why use external CSS?

External CSS keeps HTML and CSS separate, making projects cleaner, reusable, and easier to maintain.

